.TH FANDYN-CALIBRATE 8 "2026-10-22" "fandyn 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fandyn-calibrate \- one-time fan and thermal calibration for fandyn
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fandyn-calibrate
.RB [ \-\-force ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-temp
.IR C ]
.RB [ \-\-quick ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR DIR ]
.br
.B fandyn-calibrate
.BR \-\-background " | " \-\-next\-boot
.br
.B fandyn-calibrate \-\-refit
.I FILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Learns the board once and writes the fixed profile used by
.BR fandynd (8).
It is loud on purpose: for about 16 minutes it sweeps the fan through its whole
range and loads every CPU core. It measures the fan's speed curve, floor and
start-up kick; fits a lumped thermal model (heatsink capacity, fan-dependent
convection, die-to-sink resistance, ambient) by output-error least squares with
covariance estimates; designs the slowest fan curve that still holds each
temperature; then tests that profile on the board and in simulation. If the model
fails its statistical or physical checks, a safe fallback curve is used.
.PP
It runs automatically when the package is installed. A guardian process
returns the fan to the kernel if the calibrator itself dies.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-force
Recalibrate now, replacing an existing profile. Without it the calibrator
refuses to overwrite a profile.
.TP
.B \-\-background
Recalibrate now as a systemd service; follow with
.BR "journalctl \-fu fandyn-calibrate" .
.TP
.B \-\-next\-boot
Recalibrate unattended about 3 minutes after the next boot.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-temp " C"
Temperature where the fan reaches full speed (55\(en80, default 70).
.TP
.B \-\-quick
Shorter measurement (about 7 minutes, less accurate).
.TP
.BI \-o " DIR"
Output directory (default
.IR /var/lib/fandyn ).
.TP
.BI \-\-refit " FILE"
Refit the thermal model from a saved calibration.csv without touching the fan.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 calibrated and tested; 1 no fan, no access or write error; 2 profile written
with warnings or as safe fallback; 3 aborted; 4 refused (profile exists, no
.BR \-\-force ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/fandyn/profile
The fixed profile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/fandyn/calibration.csv
Every raw sample.
.TP
.I /var/lib/fandyn/report.txt
Model, statistics and test results.
.TP
.I /var/lib/fandyn/history.csv
One line per calibration.
.TP
.I /var/lib/fandyn/recalibrate
Pending recalibration request.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fandynd (8)
